WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.400
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:07.670 --> 00:09.400
I've gone and done it again.

3
00:09.400 --> 00:11.000
[RINKA: Where are you?]

4
00:11.000 --> 00:14.210
I really am unlucky. [RINKA: Don't tell me you forgot]

5
00:14.210 --> 00:16.630
Are you listening, Mr. Ichinose?

6
00:16.630 --> 00:18.990
Of course. My apologies.

7
00:18.990 --> 00:20.940
An apology won't cut it.

8
00:20.940 --> 00:22.980
Ma'am, please listen.

9
00:23.670 --> 00:27.700
Kubota, you put Miyagi in a headlock.

10
00:27.700 --> 00:30.690
It was the other child who was in the wrong.

11
00:30.690 --> 00:33.090
Akito said he was betrayed!

12
00:33.090 --> 00:35.980
He was, in a game.

13
00:36.980 --> 00:40.010
Their team lost a match in an online shooter.

14
00:40.010 --> 00:41.930
Because he sucked!

15
00:41.930 --> 00:46.230
Ma'am, could we ask you to put a stop to his gaming at night?

16
00:46.230 --> 00:48.790
A lack of sleep affects his studies, and...

17
00:48.790 --> 00:52.790
What? You're telling me I'm accountable?

18
00:52.790 --> 00:57.280
Matters that occur at school are the teacher's responsibility!

19
00:57.280 --> 01:00.400
However, we cannot monitor how your children spend their nights.

20
01:00.400 --> 01:02.990
And why is my child the only one apologizing?

21
01:02.990 --> 01:04.830
Both children engaged in the fight.

22
01:04.830 --> 01:08.820
Teachers like you always side with the victims.

23
01:18.510 --> 01:20.460
Mr. Ichinose.

24
01:27.000 --> 01:30.410
I'm terribly sorry, ma'am.

25
01:31.370 --> 01:33.690
I'm an unlucky guy.

26
01:33.690 --> 01:35.680
Ma'am...

27
01:39.140 --> 01:42.010
Come on...

28
01:42.640 --> 01:44.140
Go, go!

29
01:44.140 --> 01:47.790
You almost got it!

30
01:47.790 --> 01:49.680
[TIME UP]

31
01:49.680 --> 01:54.150
I'm confident I'm the unluckiest dude around.

32
01:54.150 --> 01:56.350
Shoot, I forgot about Rinka.

33
01:56.350 --> 01:58.320
[RINKA: Don't tell me you forgot. Hey!]

34
01:58.880 --> 02:01.090
At my previous schools...

35
02:01.090 --> 02:03.850
I understand this is your grandma's memento,

36
02:03.850 --> 02:06.680
but you don't have to bring it to school, right?

37
02:06.680 --> 02:07.620
Yeah.

38
02:07.620 --> 02:10.860
I'll hold onto it, so come get it after school.

39
02:10.860 --> 02:12.240
Okay.

40
02:13.260 --> 02:14.800
- Mr. Ichinose. - Yes?

41
02:14.800 --> 02:17.650
A student from Class 2 came to get something.

42
02:17.650 --> 02:20.590
I'll be right there.

43
02:24.300 --> 02:26.170
I just put it here.

44
02:27.040 --> 02:27.900
Where did it go?

45
02:27.900 --> 02:30.860
[Apology Regarding the Lost Brooch]

46
02:30.860 --> 02:33.510
Mr. Ichinose, please stop them!

47
02:33.510 --> 02:37.040
What are you two doing? Cut it out!

48
02:37.040 --> 02:38.550
I said, cut it out!

49
02:38.550 --> 02:41.140
- Ouch! - He hit her!

50
02:41.140 --> 02:43.630
- Are you okay? Where did you get hit? - Don't touch me!

51
02:43.630 --> 02:45.150
- Are you okay? - He touched her.

52
02:45.150 --> 02:47.420
He touched her!

53
02:47.420 --> 02:49.740
- He touched her! - It wasn't on purpose!

54
02:49.740 --> 02:53.990
You hurt my child, and touched her.

55
02:53.990 --> 02:56.500
It is a misunderstanding.

56
02:56.500 --> 02:58.880
But it's true you touched her, no?

57
02:58.880 --> 03:03.020
My daughter says she is traumatized.

58
03:09.360 --> 03:12.700
I'm terribly sorry for what I've caused.

59
03:12.700 --> 03:15.840
[Apology Regarding Unwarranted Contact]

60
03:20.910 --> 03:23.140
Mr. Ichinose stole it!

61
03:23.140 --> 03:25.130
She refuses to go to school because of you!

62
03:25.130 --> 03:27.300
- He assaulted her. - He created disciplinary issues!

63
03:27.300 --> 03:28.650
How come you punished her?

64
03:28.650 --> 03:32.150
- He touched her! - Take accountability!

65
03:34.160 --> 03:38.070
Mr. Ichinose. How about considering a transfer?

66
03:38.070 --> 03:40.240
I'm sure it's getting difficult to stay.

67
03:43.980 --> 03:46.020
[The wild Blissey ran away!]

68
03:47.000 --> 03:50.470
I've given up all ridiculous expectations.

69
03:50.470 --> 03:53.430
My sole goal at this new school, is...

70
03:54.760 --> 03:56.720
[Inoffensive]

71
03:57.490 --> 03:59.200
To be inoffensive!

72
04:03.370 --> 04:04.950
Time to go home.

73
04:14.170 --> 04:17.580
Woah, who left this here?

74
04:17.580 --> 04:19.560
Watch out!

75
04:21.390 --> 04:23.560
I'm sorry, Ms. Nashiki!

76
04:23.560 --> 04:26.690
- Are you alright? I'm so sorry! - It's fine.

77
04:27.940 --> 04:31.630
I'm sorry, it's my fault for being in the way.

78
04:47.250 --> 04:49.780
Man, I really am unlucky today.

79
04:50.700 --> 04:54.360
But I guess my luck has always been terrible.

80
04:54.360 --> 04:56.800
I caused so much trouble at my last school, too.

81
04:57.570 --> 05:00.160
Like that one time I forgot to turn off the pool pump.

82
05:00.160 --> 05:01.800
What?

83
05:01.800 --> 05:07.010
The weather took a turn, so pool day was canceled.

84
05:07.010 --> 05:11.820
Then one of my students got a fever. And it was a Friday.

85
05:11.820 --> 05:15.050
- Really, there was a lot going on. - You left it running?

86
05:15.050 --> 05:16.470
Until Monday?

87
05:16.470 --> 05:20.820
Yeah. The water bill was over a million yen.

88
05:21.350 --> 05:22.740
A million...

89
05:22.740 --> 05:28.560
The city took on half the bill. The rest, I split with the Principal.

90
05:29.150 --> 05:33.640
Still, paying out of pocket for a mistake at school... It sucked.

91
05:35.540 --> 05:39.150
Anyway, the Principal hated me after that,

92
05:39.150 --> 05:41.000
which is why I'm here now.

93
05:44.670 --> 05:49.160
You never once thought about quitting?

94
05:50.320 --> 05:54.900
I admit I've considered it.

95
05:56.510 --> 05:58.500
But, you know.

96
06:01.850 --> 06:05.810
You're very tough, Mr. Ichinose.

97
06:06.620 --> 06:08.420
You think?

98
06:10.580 --> 06:12.760
I get beaten down all the time though.

99
06:15.020 --> 06:17.680
- Here. - Thank you.

100
06:19.470 --> 06:22.210
Today sure was another rough day.

101
06:22.210 --> 06:25.930
Parents are complaining, and it's only April.

102
06:25.930 --> 06:31.250
But you don't give in.

103
06:32.760 --> 06:33.840
Well...

104
06:33.840 --> 06:38.370
Thanks to you, I could smile again for the first time today.

105
06:39.150 --> 06:41.070
See you after the break.

106
06:43.400 --> 06:44.910
Wait.

107
06:46.530 --> 06:48.760
Are you heading back to the classroom?

108
06:48.760 --> 06:51.920
Yes. I still have work to finish.

109
06:51.920 --> 06:53.630
Sorry.

110
06:54.800 --> 07:01.640
Iroha Nashiki. Another new hire who started this April like me.

111
07:02.810 --> 07:04.890
At the time, I had no idea

112
07:04.890 --> 07:10.160
she had spent the last year away from work, depressed.

113
07:24.960 --> 07:27.600
Mr. Ichinose, over here.

114
07:32.680 --> 07:34.140
Good evening.

115
07:34.140 --> 07:35.520
Thanks for coming.

116
07:35.520 --> 07:38.550
Is this everyone from Third Elementary School?

117
07:38.550 --> 07:43.610
A teacher named Nashiki was to join us, but we can proceed without her.

118
07:43.610 --> 07:46.450
- I see. Then let's get started. - Right.

119
07:46.450 --> 07:52.550
Folks, we appreciate your help in patrolling Shibuya to look out for our youth.

120
07:56.690 --> 07:58.750
I wonder where Ms. Nashiki could be.

121
07:58.750 --> 08:00.590
She didn't show, and that's that.

122
08:00.590 --> 08:02.370
Mr. Ichinose, the flag.

123
08:02.370 --> 08:03.930
Right.

124
08:39.320 --> 08:41.770
Hey, what're you guys doing out this late?

125
08:41.770 --> 08:43.940
Don't worry, I got this.

126
08:43.940 --> 08:45.150
You're high schoolers, right?

127
08:45.150 --> 08:46.720
Who is this man?

128
08:46.720 --> 08:48.800
- My father. Right? - Y-Yes.

129
08:48.800 --> 08:50.040
See?

130
08:50.040 --> 08:51.790
Your "father", is it?

131
08:51.790 --> 08:54.470
- What's the problem? - I doubt it.

132
09:07.860 --> 09:12.080
Hey, aren't you guys elementary schoolers?

133
09:12.080 --> 09:13.510
It's already way past 8PM.

134
09:13.510 --> 09:18.320
Tonight, a comet last visible 341 years ago in 1685,

135
09:18.320 --> 09:20.980
will grace our skies once more.

136
09:21.910 --> 09:24.800
This shot was taken this morning at 5AM,

137
09:24.800 --> 09:28.110
using four different cameras across Tokyo.

138
09:28.110 --> 09:30.960
Zoom into the northern sky, and you will see...

139
09:30.960 --> 09:32.860
Ready?

140
09:33.900 --> 09:35.910
What are you doing?

141
09:36.730 --> 09:38.590
They said they'd go home if I joined...

142
09:38.590 --> 09:40.060
Get out.

143
09:40.060 --> 09:42.230
- Aw, come on. - I'm calling your parents.

144
09:42.230 --> 09:44.530
- Let us have our picture! - No.

145
09:44.530 --> 09:47.100
- Why not? - Do you realize what time it is?

146
09:50.370 --> 09:53.820
- Why didn't you scold them? - Five, four,

147
09:55.250 --> 09:57.000
- Sorry. - three, two, one!

148
09:59.140 --> 10:00.910
Nice photo.

149
10:00.910 --> 10:03.370
- We're leaving. - Right.

150
10:41.850 --> 10:44.900
I pray nothing eventful happens tomorrow.

151
10:50.800 --> 10:53.180
To be inoffensive is the safest option.

152
10:53.180 --> 10:56.140
I want to avoid conflict at all costs.

153
10:56.140 --> 11:02.950
We will be seeing the same sky as our Edo ancestors, 341 years ago.

154
11:02.950 --> 11:07.490
- A comet. - The Knox Comet, visible every 120 years.

155
11:07.490 --> 11:12.960
Though tonight is a cloudy night, perhaps we can see the comet peek through.

156
11:12.960 --> 11:16.740
Now, for our next headline.

157
11:28.000 --> 11:30.570
Seriously?

158
11:30.570 --> 11:33.140
This can't be happening.

159
11:39.940 --> 11:42.580
Damn it!

160
12:04.850 --> 12:06.650
Please, wait!

161
12:08.180 --> 12:09.710
Calm down.

162
12:09.710 --> 12:12.840
I'll be right over there.

163
12:23.600 --> 12:25.410
Ms. Nashiki?

164
12:26.450 --> 12:29.020
That's you, isn't it?

165
12:29.020 --> 12:30.260
But why?

166
12:30.260 --> 12:33.680
- Mr. Ichinose... - No! Don't move!

167
12:34.690 --> 12:35.840
Don't move.

168
12:35.840 --> 12:38.460
I'll be right over there.

169
12:42.080 --> 12:45.200
Ms. Nashiki, your hand.

170
13:08.330 --> 13:11.970
God! I don't care if I'm unlucky for life!

171
13:11.970 --> 13:15.190
Just please, give me this one chance!

172
13:31.320 --> 13:34.250
Ms. Nashiki! Your hand!

173
13:59.490 --> 14:01.220
She's alive.

174
14:09.560 --> 14:11.500
Please, wait!

175
14:16.420 --> 14:18.420
Where the hell am I?

176
14:19.350 --> 14:21.420
Ms. Nashiki?

177
14:21.420 --> 14:25.460
Is this paradise?

178
14:25.460 --> 14:27.250
What?

179
14:27.250 --> 14:29.360
Ms. Nashiki, did you hit your head somewhere?

180
14:31.590 --> 14:33.520
Who the hell are you?

181
14:33.520 --> 14:35.220
- What? - State your name!

182
14:35.220 --> 14:37.940
I'm your coworker, Ikuru Ichinose.

183
14:37.940 --> 14:39.670
What's wrong?

184
14:39.670 --> 14:42.210
And why are you talking like that?

185
14:42.210 --> 14:44.600
The hell's going on?

186
14:44.600 --> 14:48.490
Where the hell am I?

187
14:48.490 --> 14:50.960
Is this an illusion?

188
14:50.960 --> 14:52.400
Ms. Nashiki?

189
14:55.400 --> 14:59.430
Screw off!

190
15:09.270 --> 15:12.710
[Episode 1]

191
15:14.310 --> 15:18.110
Excuse me, I'm not exactly following...

192
15:19.680 --> 15:21.110
Should I call an ambulance?

193
15:21.110 --> 15:23.240
The hell are you talking about?

194
15:23.980 --> 15:26.730
Wait, where's my plaque?

195
15:26.730 --> 15:27.600
Huh?

196
15:27.600 --> 15:30.060
Master Seki's geometry plaque!

197
15:30.060 --> 15:32.820
I was just looking at it!

198
15:32.820 --> 15:35.390
You weren't looking at anything.

199
15:35.390 --> 15:37.650
You were trying to jump.

200
15:37.650 --> 15:39.000
Hands off!

201
15:39.000 --> 15:40.640
Sorry!

202
15:41.420 --> 15:44.260
What happened to you?

203
15:44.260 --> 15:46.840
- It's me, Ichinose. - The hell's your problem?

204
15:46.840 --> 15:49.240
Creep.

205
15:50.330 --> 15:52.310
Sorry.

206
15:52.310 --> 15:56.320
How dare you claim a surname when you're no warrior?

207
15:56.320 --> 15:59.750
And that odd attire.

208
15:59.750 --> 16:02.030
Quit acting so familiar with me!

209
16:02.030 --> 16:03.570
Sorry.

210
16:05.480 --> 16:09.670
The hell am I wearing?

211
16:09.670 --> 16:13.550
It feels too breezy.

212
16:13.550 --> 16:15.050
Do not take it off!

213
16:15.050 --> 16:18.220
Where's my kimono? And my netsuke?

214
16:18.220 --> 16:20.320
You weren't wearing a kimono!

215
16:20.320 --> 16:21.860
This isn't the Edo period.

216
16:21.860 --> 16:23.920
Edo period? What's that?

217
16:23.920 --> 16:25.680
It's the period of Edo, what else?

218
16:25.680 --> 16:27.600
Aren't you a certified teacher, Ms. Nashiki?

219
16:27.600 --> 16:30.450
Who's this "Ms. Nashiki" you keep talking about?

220
16:32.520 --> 16:36.350
You. You, Iroha Nashiki.

221
16:38.940 --> 16:40.990
Quit your ridiculous talk.

222
16:40.990 --> 16:43.790
I'm no warrior. I have no surname!

223
16:43.790 --> 16:45.430
- What? - Listen well.

224
16:45.430 --> 16:48.490
I come from a family of couriers.

225
16:48.490 --> 16:51.900
"A great mountain road intersects the Shibuya and Uda rivers."

226
16:51.900 --> 16:56.330
"Delivering from Edo's Akasaka to Isehara,

227
16:56.330 --> 17:01.900
people call us, the Tokubei Couriers!"

228
17:04.410 --> 17:06.460
You sound like you're from the Edo period.

229
17:06.460 --> 17:09.790
- And what's that? - The period of Edo!

230
17:09.790 --> 17:11.900
The one before Meiji? Tell me you've heard of Tokugawa.

231
17:11.900 --> 17:14.730
'Course I know the Tokugawa Family!

232
17:14.730 --> 17:18.740
Lord Tsunayoshi became the 5th shogun just the other day.

233
17:18.740 --> 17:21.540
Tsunayoshi. Known for instituting animal welfare laws.

234
17:21.540 --> 17:24.190
The year, 1685. [1685 - The Rescued Hachiko]

235
17:24.190 --> 17:27.790
1685? That's 341 years ago!

236
17:27.790 --> 17:29.780
Hey, what gives?

237
17:30.520 --> 17:32.980
I refuse to accept this is happening.

238
17:32.980 --> 17:35.520
In other words...

239
17:35.520 --> 17:39.500
We will be seeing the same sky as our Edo ancestors.

240
17:39.500 --> 17:41.460
The comet?

241
17:45.130 --> 17:49.280
No, calm down. This is your unluckiest incident yet.

242
17:49.280 --> 17:52.620
This really does look like paradise.

243
17:52.620 --> 17:55.980
It's like I was born to be unlucky.

244
17:55.980 --> 18:00.020
But why is she speaking like she's from 341 years ago?

245
18:00.650 --> 18:03.720
Hey, are you alright?

246
18:03.720 --> 18:06.610
Can it be? Did she really time travel...

247
18:06.610 --> 18:09.270
No, no, no!

248
18:09.270 --> 18:12.460
I'm not falling for your tricks, Ms. Nashiki.

249
18:12.460 --> 18:13.580
Huh?

250
18:13.580 --> 18:17.280
There are still other possibilities.

251
18:17.280 --> 18:20.270
Let's explore our most realistic options.

252
18:20.270 --> 18:22.800
Possibilities?

253
18:23.950 --> 18:26.500
- Hey! - Sorry, can I look through this?

254
18:26.500 --> 18:28.610
- Huh? - Okay, I am.

255
18:32.710 --> 18:34.670
"Iroha Nashiki".

256
18:34.670 --> 18:38.830
See, look. This is your face, isn't it?

257
18:40.930 --> 18:42.870
My face?

258
18:45.800 --> 18:47.480
Do I need to repeat myself?

259
18:47.480 --> 18:52.100
I'm Iroha, daughter to the Tokubei Couriers. I have no surname!

260
18:53.740 --> 18:55.370
Okay, now I'm sure.

261
18:56.270 --> 19:00.950
I knew we were both heading towards the deep end.

262
19:00.950 --> 19:07.430
Though I know you both went through some troubles at your previous schools,

263
19:07.430 --> 19:12.990
I hope this school will provide a fresh start for you both.

264
19:16.240 --> 19:18.950
- Looking forward to your guidance. - Pleased to meet you all.

265
19:18.950 --> 19:23.400
Ms. Nashiki. Louder, if you could.

266
19:24.750 --> 19:27.280
Pleased to meet you all.

267
19:27.280 --> 19:30.090
We've both finally lost it.

268
19:30.090 --> 19:32.960
- Huh? - Didn't you feel that odd sensation earlier?

269
19:32.960 --> 19:36.720
It was like space warped so I could catch you.

270
19:38.120 --> 19:43.530
I don't even know why I'm here. It's like I'm trapped in an illusion.

271
19:43.530 --> 19:45.410
What a nightmare.

272
19:45.410 --> 19:51.090
Exactly, that feeling of a dream. It means we're avoiding reality.

273
19:51.090 --> 19:55.140
Either way, the cause of all this is stress.

274
19:55.140 --> 19:57.450
- Stress? - Yeah.

275
19:58.060 --> 20:02.410
And right after I found another school...

276
20:02.410 --> 20:03.740
Guess I'll go see a therapist.

277
20:03.740 --> 20:08.040
Tell me, how do I wake up from this dream?

278
20:08.040 --> 20:10.660
How do I go back home?

279
20:15.110 --> 20:18.680
Get in. Or else you can't go down.

280
20:26.740 --> 20:31.250
I hope this is just a nightmare.

281
20:35.640 --> 20:37.310
You shut us in here!

282
20:37.310 --> 20:39.650
Bastard!

283
20:41.400 --> 20:43.160
The hell?

284
20:43.160 --> 20:44.270
What's going on?

285
20:44.270 --> 20:48.260
I mean, what am I supposed to do?

286
20:55.520 --> 20:57.730
What are you doing?

287
21:01.340 --> 21:03.850
You're shaking, too.

288
21:12.110 --> 21:18.270
No matter how unlucky I may be, this is simply unheard of.

289
21:21.530 --> 21:23.010
Ms. Nashiki.

290
21:24.720 --> 21:27.070
What in the world?

291
21:32.750 --> 21:34.000
Is that a monster?

292
21:34.000 --> 21:35.420
Ms. Nashiki!

293
21:35.420 --> 21:36.880
Sorry!

294
21:42.990 --> 21:45.910
You okay? Are you drunk?

295
21:45.910 --> 21:48.070
Hands off, you bastard!

296
21:48.070 --> 21:50.680
Ms. Nashiki! Stop that!

297
21:51.520 --> 21:53.340
- Keep her in check! - Sorry! She's drunk!

298
21:53.340 --> 21:55.440
- Crazy chick! - I'm not drunk!

299
21:55.440 --> 21:56.850
Calm down, please!

300
21:56.850 --> 21:58.770
I'll call for a taxi right away.

301
21:58.770 --> 22:01.520
- Taxi! - Wait.

302
22:02.550 --> 22:07.070
I can trust you, right?

303
22:07.760 --> 22:13.540
Yes. At the very least, I'm acting with your best interest in mind.

304
22:19.530 --> 22:23.500
So bright at this time of night...

305
22:23.500 --> 22:26.430
This really is like a dream.

306
22:29.940 --> 22:34.470
Is this place like the Dragon Palace?

307
22:34.470 --> 22:38.970
The Dragon Palace? From Urashima Taro?

308
22:39.840 --> 22:41.880
Woah.

309
22:41.880 --> 22:44.810
This place is no paradise like that.

310
22:44.810 --> 22:48.360
Wish I could tell Ma and Pa about this.

311
22:48.360 --> 22:51.140
So long as 300 years don't pass

312
22:51.140 --> 22:56.760
while I'm gone like Urashima Taro though.

313
22:56.760 --> 23:00.240
Sorry, you've actually skipped 341 years.

314
23:01.200 --> 23:08.550
Hold on. If she really is someone else right now,

315
23:10.340 --> 23:14.640
where is this Iroha Nashiki?

316
23:18.380 --> 23:20.030
Thank you.

317
23:20.570 --> 23:21.960
- Do you need a receipt? - No, thank you.

318
23:21.960 --> 23:24.400
- Of course. Get back safely. - Where is this place?

319
23:25.070 --> 23:27.200
- I can't get out! - Hold on.

320
23:33.350 --> 23:35.790
This is supposedly your home, Ms. Nashiki.

321
23:35.790 --> 23:39.090
The hell is that?

322
23:39.090 --> 23:40.920
Tell me, what is it?

323
23:44.150 --> 23:45.770
This is your room.

324
23:48.170 --> 23:49.880
Here, your keys.

325
23:49.880 --> 23:52.210
Huh? What's this?

326
23:52.210 --> 23:54.190
Do you not lock up behind you?

327
23:54.190 --> 23:57.710
'Course I do. With my trusty door bar.

328
23:57.710 --> 24:00.550
Well, think of this as the modern "door bar".

329
24:00.550 --> 24:05.100
How's that supposed to...

330
24:05.100 --> 24:06.500
Huh?

331
24:07.470 --> 24:08.960
Go on.

332
24:13.300 --> 24:15.320
Please excuse me.

333
24:22.690 --> 24:25.940
It stinks in here.

334
24:27.350 --> 24:29.040
Remember anything?

335
24:29.040 --> 24:30.450
No.

336
24:31.450 --> 24:35.620
Well now, what to do...

337
24:37.540 --> 24:41.000
This turns the light on and off.

338
24:49.650 --> 24:52.530
- Stop that. - Sorry.

339
24:53.180 --> 24:56.610
Since it'd be a ruckus taking this out at night,

340
24:56.610 --> 24:58.440
take this garbage to the lot in the morning.

341
24:58.440 --> 25:00.890
- The lot? - Yes.

342
25:02.100 --> 25:03.750
Sorry in advance.

343
25:06.320 --> 25:08.770
This seems to be your bath room.

344
25:10.670 --> 25:11.770
Take your shoes off!

345
25:11.770 --> 25:14.740
I thought we had dirt floors!

346
25:20.600 --> 25:22.240
This is your restroom.

347
25:22.240 --> 25:25.360
The wash closet, if you will.

348
25:25.360 --> 25:26.880
Turn this, and it'll flush.

349
25:26.880 --> 25:29.600
Woah!

350
25:29.600 --> 25:32.850
It produces water without going to a well?

351
25:32.850 --> 25:34.960
You have hot water, too. Here's the boiler.

352
25:34.960 --> 25:37.190
Hot water?

353
25:37.190 --> 25:39.640
Give it a whirl later.

354
25:39.640 --> 25:42.250
- I'll continue with my explanation. - Alright.

355
25:42.250 --> 25:44.000
This is your kitchen.

356
25:44.000 --> 25:46.340
You'll do your cooking here.

357
25:47.410 --> 25:49.210
And this is how you get fire.

358
25:50.530 --> 25:52.180
How did you do that?

359
25:53.070 --> 25:54.650
You press here.

360
26:00.340 --> 26:05.370
This has to be magic.

361
26:06.150 --> 26:08.040
I'll keep the flame on low.

362
26:08.040 --> 26:11.050
You most likely have pots and pans in a cabinet there.

363
26:11.050 --> 26:14.190
Here is your bag.

364
26:14.190 --> 26:16.730
Your wallet is in there, too.

365
26:16.730 --> 26:19.180
Then I'll be heading out.

366
26:21.280 --> 26:23.260
Hey, wait.

367
26:23.260 --> 26:26.340
- You're leaving? - Why would I stay?

368
26:26.340 --> 26:29.420
You live here, by yourself I presume.

369
26:29.420 --> 26:32.860
Women live alone?

370
26:32.860 --> 26:35.120
Yeah. It's not so unheard of nowadays.

371
26:35.120 --> 26:38.510
Especially since both men and women work.

372
26:47.400 --> 26:51.930
Ms. Nashiki and I are both elementary school teachers.

373
26:55.600 --> 26:57.050
[Third Grade Math]

374
26:59.320 --> 27:01.940
[Third Grade Math]

375
27:11.410 --> 27:14.380
Confucius says, they who know the truth...

376
27:14.380 --> 27:15.410
Sorry!

377
27:15.410 --> 27:19.680
are not equal to those who love it, and they who love it

378
27:19.680 --> 27:22.480
are not equal to those who delight in it.

379
27:22.480 --> 27:29.480
Those who are keen to learn, excel over those with knowledge.

380
27:32.960 --> 27:39.410
And those who find joy in learning, rise above them all.

381
27:40.060 --> 27:43.790
In other words, I am talking about her!

382
27:45.160 --> 27:48.100
This is Iroha, of the Tokubei Couriers.

383
27:48.100 --> 27:52.350
Her passion for math triumphs that of some of our smartest warriors.

384
27:52.350 --> 27:54.160
Master Seki, that is a bit...

385
27:54.160 --> 27:56.620
But master, she is a commoner!

386
27:56.620 --> 27:58.190
A commoner, besting a warrior?

387
27:58.190 --> 28:00.850
Education has no such boundaries.

388
28:00.850 --> 28:03.130
Then can you solve this question?

389
28:04.900 --> 28:09.890
Let's see. "There are a total of 60 pheasants and rabbits,

390
28:09.890 --> 28:12.500
with a total count of 150 feet."

391
28:12.500 --> 28:16.210
Ah, the pheasant and rabbit problem.

392
28:16.210 --> 28:20.250
You would use an area calculation for this.

393
28:20.250 --> 28:22.020
First and foremost...

394
28:24.040 --> 28:30.330
Is this a booklet teaching mathematics?

395
28:30.330 --> 28:32.160
Yes.

396
28:32.790 --> 28:34.420
We just call it math nowadays.

397
28:34.420 --> 28:38.370
And this is beginners mathematics. They teach this to young warriors.

398
28:38.370 --> 28:39.760
Makes sense.

399
28:39.760 --> 28:44.530
An elementary school teacher would teach to a similar age range.

400
28:47.550 --> 28:50.540
- What? - Can it be...

401
28:50.540 --> 28:53.150
Can it really be?

402
28:53.150 --> 28:56.700
Master Seki, is that for your next lecture?

403
28:56.700 --> 28:58.610
May I see?

404
29:02.050 --> 29:04.690
You truly are passionate.

405
29:06.700 --> 29:08.250
My apologies, sir.

406
29:08.250 --> 29:12.180
- Why apologize? - I have no need to look at such documents.

407
29:12.180 --> 29:15.880
Why? You love mathematics.

408
29:15.880 --> 29:17.380
Yes.

409
29:17.970 --> 29:22.700
However, liking the subject won't change a thing.

410
29:22.700 --> 29:25.880
A young woman cannot open a school.

411
29:25.880 --> 29:28.050
People would never accept such a thing.

412
29:28.690 --> 29:32.100
Ah, the public opinion.

413
29:32.780 --> 29:35.830
But is that any reason to give up your passion?

414
29:38.960 --> 29:45.700
Year 8 of the Keicho Era. Before the Tokugawa brought peace to Edo,

415
29:45.700 --> 29:51.980
a period of war and bloodshed lasted for 150 years.

416
29:51.980 --> 29:53.420
Yes.

417
29:54.310 --> 29:58.210
There is no such thing as unchanging in this world.

418
29:59.790 --> 30:02.850
People change as do the seasons.

419
30:02.850 --> 30:06.330
And so do their values.

420
30:06.330 --> 30:08.980
But, Iroha.

421
30:10.650 --> 30:12.650
You mustn't change for them.

422
30:13.530 --> 30:18.150
Your fun and your enjoyment is yours to keep.

423
30:18.930 --> 30:22.810
You must never give up your love for mathematics.

424
30:23.520 --> 30:25.850
Devote yourself to it.

425
30:25.850 --> 30:29.160
One day, this world will change.

426
30:29.810 --> 30:31.620
So you'll fight on.

427
30:34.410 --> 30:38.780
Yes, Master Seki.

428
30:38.780 --> 30:46.410
Is this an age where women like me can become teachers as well?

429
30:47.960 --> 30:53.760
Of course. They can become teachers for children, teens, and young adults.

430
30:53.760 --> 30:56.000
Man or woman has nothing to do with it.

431
30:58.280 --> 31:00.120
I see.

432
31:03.590 --> 31:06.070
I see.

433
31:12.010 --> 31:16.020
However, Ms. Nashiki...

434
31:17.740 --> 31:20.530
I don't think she would have lasted long.

435
31:22.080 --> 31:25.590
She stayed at school from dawn till almost midnight,

436
31:26.590 --> 31:29.220
and still had work left over.

437
31:35.800 --> 31:38.160
[1st Grade - Language Studies]

438
31:38.160 --> 31:40.520
[6th Grade - Sciences]

439
31:47.960 --> 31:50.240
These dates...

440
31:50.240 --> 31:51.440
No way. [June, Week One]

441
31:51.440 --> 31:53.040
What?

442
31:54.960 --> 31:58.830
She made daily curriculums for the entire year.

443
31:58.830 --> 32:00.690
For this subject.

444
32:00.690 --> 32:02.230
And this one, too.

445
32:02.230 --> 32:05.220
Did she have one planned for every grade?

446
32:06.310 --> 32:08.170
Is that amazing?

447
32:08.170 --> 32:09.500
It's beyond amazing.

448
32:09.500 --> 32:12.280
This amount of prep would take an absurd amount of time.

449
32:12.280 --> 32:14.820
No one would normally put in this amount of effort.

450
32:21.980 --> 32:24.040
Ms. Nashiki...

451
32:26.300 --> 32:28.990
She worked hard.

452
32:28.990 --> 32:33.110
She wanted to make sure she was ready to teach,

453
32:33.110 --> 32:37.590
no matter what sort of extra work came her way.

454
32:39.040 --> 32:43.950
She prepared so much, and yet...

455
32:44.680 --> 32:46.290
She crumbled.

456
32:46.290 --> 32:47.940
Why?

457
32:50.300 --> 32:54.120
Teaching nowadays is a strange job.

458
32:55.040 --> 32:59.600
Not only do we teach, but we act as substitute parents as well.

459
32:59.600 --> 33:06.320
Things parents ought to teach their kids, have now become our responsibility.

460
33:06.320 --> 33:09.720
And if something goes wrong, all the blame falls on the teacher.

461
33:09.720 --> 33:14.440
The principal, Board of Education, board of directors, PTA...

462
33:14.440 --> 33:17.190
Us teachers can only nod, and obey their orders.

463
33:18.860 --> 33:23.260
We have to kill ourselves to work.

464
33:24.810 --> 33:27.120
What the hell?

465
33:28.050 --> 33:30.620
The absolute nerve!

466
33:31.510 --> 33:36.860
Teaching is not a job to look down on.

467
33:36.860 --> 33:42.400
Do you realize how special a role it is?

468
33:44.550 --> 33:48.630
Confucius teaches "Heaven, Earth, Sovereign, Ancestors, and Teachers".

469
33:48.630 --> 33:52.050
They are five elements, in a balance.

470
33:52.050 --> 33:56.750
And we are taught to respect each as equals.

471
33:56.750 --> 33:59.570
When a parent leaves their child with a teacher,

472
33:59.570 --> 34:05.240
they plead with all their might, that you will guide them well.

473
34:05.240 --> 34:08.120
That is how important your role is.

474
34:08.120 --> 34:10.610
Discipline is to be taught by the parent.

475
34:10.610 --> 34:16.050
While teachers guide their students to becoming proper adults.

476
34:16.700 --> 34:21.340
That is why teaching is such a special job.

477
34:21.950 --> 34:24.400
Status be damned.

478
34:24.400 --> 34:28.230
Everyone is to respect a teacher.

479
34:28.230 --> 34:31.490
How to praise or scold their child is up to the teacher,

480
34:31.490 --> 34:33.500
the parents have no say in this.

481
34:33.500 --> 34:38.300
That is what it means to entrust your child to a teacher.

482
34:39.980 --> 34:42.100
And yet, you.

483
34:42.940 --> 34:45.480
You're a coward.

484
34:45.480 --> 34:49.530
How can you be so complacent? Stand your ground.

485
34:49.530 --> 34:52.430
Or don't you dare call yourself a teacher!

486
34:55.490 --> 34:57.650
What would you know?

487
34:59.900 --> 35:02.950
That just won't fly nowadays.

488
35:04.930 --> 35:07.440
A teacher paves the way for a kid's future.

489
35:07.980 --> 35:10.700
You think I don't know that?

490
35:10.700 --> 35:14.580
But teaching isn't the only job we have at school.

491
35:14.580 --> 35:17.980
Miscellaneous work endlessly piles up on us.

492
35:18.740 --> 35:22.300
You think I'm so misguided, but I...

493
35:26.060 --> 35:28.380
I became a teacher because I wanted to.

494
35:28.380 --> 35:32.210
I wanted to become a teacher who would leave an impression on kids.

495
35:34.760 --> 35:36.310
But...

496
35:38.700 --> 35:40.970
So did I.

497
35:42.270 --> 35:45.620
It was my lifelong dream.

498
35:53.030 --> 35:54.790
Can't I do it?

499
35:56.600 --> 36:02.800
Can't I take Iroha Nashiki's place, and become a teacher?

500
36:02.800 --> 36:04.600
That'd be impossible.

501
36:04.600 --> 36:06.850
Our eras don't even use the same alphabet.

502
36:06.850 --> 36:09.240
Then I'll just learn what I don't know.

503
36:09.840 --> 36:14.690
I'll become the teacher she wanted to be.

504
36:15.880 --> 36:20.830
Where is the original Ms. Nashiki?

505
36:20.830 --> 36:22.800
Beats me.

506
36:23.430 --> 36:26.600
I don't even know why I'm here myself.

507
36:27.390 --> 36:31.950
But if this is no dream,

508
36:31.950 --> 36:34.170
if this is really happening,

509
36:35.030 --> 36:37.990
then I've got no choice but to live on.

510
36:39.550 --> 36:43.080
Although, with how suddenly this happened,

511
36:43.620 --> 36:46.740
things might suddenly go back to normal, too.

512
36:46.740 --> 36:50.060
That's when Iroha Nashiki will return.

513
36:51.530 --> 36:53.220
Right back here.

514
36:58.530 --> 37:02.980
Can we wait a night first?

515
37:03.890 --> 37:10.460
This might all be a dream once we wake up.

516
37:12.260 --> 37:15.330
I'm going to head home.

517
37:15.330 --> 37:18.730
Make a cup of tea for yourself, and get comfortable.

518
37:18.730 --> 37:20.330
Good night.

519
37:31.180 --> 37:34.690
You made the right call.

520
37:37.980 --> 37:43.040
You decided, didn't you? Don't get involved.

521
37:46.290 --> 37:49.010
Make tea?

522
37:55.900 --> 38:00.900
I think he pressed this for fire...

523
38:03.900 --> 38:05.660
A bit small, isn't it?

524
38:51.260 --> 38:52.940
I know.

525
38:58.970 --> 39:00.650
What do I do...

526
39:35.580 --> 39:37.220
Get back!

527
39:42.620 --> 39:44.080
Why?

528
39:44.080 --> 39:45.830
Now is not the time!

529
39:50.830 --> 39:53.240
- The fire! - Damn it!

530
39:53.240 --> 39:55.190
Work with me here!

531
39:55.650 --> 39:57.090
Damn it...

532
40:55.500 --> 40:58.960
- This is awful. - What the heck?

533
40:58.960 --> 41:02.110
This is awesome!

534
41:02.850 --> 41:06.220
Look! Wow...

535
41:06.220 --> 41:09.830
Like cherry blossom colored snowflakes!

536
41:12.080 --> 41:15.170
What is her deal?

537
41:15.170 --> 41:17.120
It sure is pretty!

538
41:23.200 --> 41:25.450
She...

539
41:25.450 --> 41:30.240
She's having a blast despite my bad luck.

540
41:33.830 --> 41:37.940
I'm sorry, it's my fault for being in the way.

541
41:40.280 --> 41:42.820
[100 points - Amazing job!]

542
41:52.130 --> 41:54.400
- Here. - Thank you.

543
42:13.440 --> 42:15.220
Thank goodness...

544
42:21.340 --> 42:23.630
Want to give it a try?

545
42:23.630 --> 42:26.500
All the textbooks and notes are safe.

546
42:26.500 --> 42:30.880
Maybe my unlucky streak doesn't affect you.

547
42:30.880 --> 42:33.750
What do you mean?

548
42:33.750 --> 42:35.540
Nothing.

549
42:36.500 --> 42:38.900
Make sure you grab all the notebooks.

550
42:45.190 --> 42:47.340
- Where are we going? - My house.

551
42:47.340 --> 42:50.740
- Huh? - You have nowhere else to go, right?

552
42:51.670 --> 42:55.150
And you're not well-versed in our current world either.

553
42:56.620 --> 43:01.550
In any case, you must live your life as "Ms. Nashiki" for now.

554
43:02.740 --> 43:09.010
Does that mean... I can be a teacher?

555
43:16.590 --> 43:20.570
I can't guarantee how long it'll last though.

556
43:20.570 --> 43:24.280
That's fine. I don't care.

557
43:24.280 --> 43:26.200
Until that end comes, I'll do it.

558
43:38.580 --> 43:40.220
Come on.

559
43:44.080 --> 43:46.550
I've got absolutely rotten luck.

560
43:46.550 --> 43:50.700
I'm positive I'm the unluckiest guy around.

561
43:50.700 --> 43:52.470
I'm leaving you behind.

562
43:52.470 --> 43:54.940
Give me time, will you?

563
44:14.920 --> 44:17.120
Come on, let's go.

564
44:17.120 --> 44:21.850
But from now on, something might change.

565
44:21.850 --> 44:26.130
- Do you know where we're going? - Of course not.

566
44:32.890 --> 44:35.310
I'll call a taxi! Wait!

567
44:36.600 --> 44:39.540
Are you listening?

568
44:52.740 --> 44:55.090
Master Seki.

569
44:57.440 --> 45:00.060
Master Seki!

570
45:00.060 --> 45:01.970
Master Seki!

571
45:01.970 --> 45:03.360
What an invigorating presence!

572
45:03.360 --> 45:06.000
Master Seki! Welcome, welcome.

573
45:06.000 --> 45:09.930
I had requested Iroha to assist with teaching today. Is she in?

574
45:09.930 --> 45:12.450
Huh? She isn't with you?

575
45:12.450 --> 45:15.760
- No. - I wonder where she's wandered off to.

576
45:15.760 --> 45:18.510
I assumed she was with you, Master Seki.

577
45:18.510 --> 45:22.060
That fool. Where has she run off to?

578
45:22.060 --> 45:24.200
How strange...

579
45:24.200 --> 45:27.550
She would never break a promise.

580
45:50.990 --> 45:52.510
Iroha?
